# Terminology

## Syntax and Conventions {#sec:syntax-and-conventions}

### Special Terms {#sec:special-terms}

The key words "MUST", "MUST NOT", "REQUIRED", "SHALL", "SHALL NOT", "SHOULD", "SHOULD NOT", "RECOMMENDED", "NOT RECOMMENDED", "MAY", and "OPTIONAL" in this document are to be interpreted as described in [[BCP 14](https://tools.ietf.org/html/bcp14)] \[[RFC2119](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2119)\] \[[RFC8174](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc8174)\] when they appear.


### Number Radix {#sec:number-radix}

This document may represent some numbers in non-decimal radix.  In these cases, the following radix notations are used:

: {.plain}
|                    |                                                                                       |
|:-------------------|:--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| 4'b0001            | Binary representation of the decimal value 1 explicitly expressed in 4 bits.          |
| 0x5A               | Hexadecimal representation of the decimal value 90.                                   |
| 7'h5A              | Hexadecimal representation of the decimal value 90 explicitly expressed in 7 bits.    |

::: NOTE
An underscore (i.e., '_') is sometimes used in the representation to improve readability.  For example, an underscore can be used in a Hexadecimal number to separate each four digits in the example:  0x0001_2345.
:::

